.TH IOWATCHD.CONF 5 "October 2026" "iowatchd 0.3.1" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
iowatchd.conf \- configuration file for iowatchd
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fI/etc/iowatchd.conf\fR is read by \fBiowatchd\fR(8). It consists of
\fBkey = value\fR lines. Blank lines are ignored and \fB#\fR starts a comment.
All keys are optional. Unknown keys and invalid values are reported as warnings
(see \fBiowatchd \-\-check\-config\fR); an invalid value never replaces the
default. Command-line options override the file. Send \fBSIGHUP\fR to reload.
.PP
After the main file, every \fI<file>.d/*.conf\fR (for example
\fI/etc/iowatchd.conf.d/10-local.conf\fR) is read in alphabetical order and
overrides earlier values. The main file can be chosen with \fB\-c\fR or
\fB$IOWATCHD_CONFIG\fR.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B device
Disk name as in \fI/proc/diskstats\fR (\fBsda\fR, \fBnvme0n1\fR). \fBauto\fR
(default) selects the physical disk holding \fI/\fR.
.TP
.B threshold
IO usage in % (1-100) that triggers a report. Default 80.
.TP
.B clear_threshold
IO usage in % below which IO is considered normal again. Default 70.
.TP
.B interval
Seconds between samples (>= 1). Default 2.
.TP
.B trigger_samples
Consecutive samples at or above the threshold before the first report. Default 2.
.TP
.B process_window
Seconds used to measure per-process IO. Default 1.
.TP
.B top_n
Number of processes in each report. Default 5.
.TP
.B cooldown
Minimum seconds between reports while IO stays high. Default 10.
.TP
.B log_file
Log file path; empty disables file logging. Default \fI/var/log/iowatchd.log\fR.
.TP
.B log_max_mb
Size in MB before rotating to \fI<file>.1\fR. \fB0\fR disables built-in
rotation (use \fBlogrotate\fR(8)). Default 5.
.TP
.B log_format
\fBtext\fR (default) or \fBjson\fR.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
device = auto
threshold = 90
log_format = json
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR iowatchd (8),
.BR iowatchd-log (1)
